%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d0e06f179b05a9346a618d4dc0a79844, type: 3}
  m_Name: SecondTutorial
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FoolsBrand.UI.TutorialSequence
  <Tutorials>k__BackingField:
  - <AdvanceCondition>k__BackingField: 3
    <TutorialText>k__BackingField: If you don't need a die right now, you can click
      on it to reserve it.  Try reserving one now by interacting with one of your
      die. If you want your dice back just reserve another die.
  - <AdvanceCondition>k__BackingField: 0
    <TutorialText>k__BackingField: 'Most enemies have more than one part you can
      choose to attack. Deciding which part to go for is crucial if you want to live
      until the end. '
  - <AdvanceCondition>k__BackingField: 1
    <TutorialText>k__BackingField: Different limbs have different defenses<sprite
      name="Defense">, which subtract from the amount of damage taken.  Pick which
      limb you want to attack, I'd suggest the eye.
  - <AdvanceCondition>k__BackingField: 0
    <TutorialText>k__BackingField: Interesting choice, hope it was a good one. Good
      luck on killing this one!
